                                                                                                                "records"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000040
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000040> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> ,
                                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001005> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A specification which is formalised and concise."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Eine Spezifikation welche formalisiert und präzise ist."@de ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0833-7989> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schema_(Informatik)> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/schema#English> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/metadata-schema> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "A schema can take many forms with different levels of formality (i.e. from ad-hoc to highly formalised), but the intent is to have a regular and systematic approach to the description of a data structure. A digital schema is often expressed in a formal language (e.g. XML, JSON) such that data can be parsed and validated automatically according to the schema. Alternatively, they might be diagrammatic or illustrative like a schema for a relational database management system."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Schema"@de ,
                                                                   "schema"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "Schemas"@de ,
                                                                                                                "Schemata"@de ,
                                                                                                                "Schemen"@de ,
                                                                                                                "schemata"@en ,
                                                                                                                "schemes"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Schema"@de ,
                                                                                                                "schema"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000041
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000041> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "OBSOLETE An entity which is structured."@en ,
                                                                                                     "OBSOLETE Eine Entität, die strukturiert ist."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#consider> <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000005> ,
                                                                                                                <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000118> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000141> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/structure> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Structure> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/structure> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.duden.de/rechtschreibung/Struktur> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/structure> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> "struct"@en ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Structures may be intentional or incidental, relations might be defined explicitly or be implicit. Structures may have only two elements or components, and these may be of different kinds. An entity serving as a frame/scaffold (one component) holding a single entity (another component) meets this definition. TODO: see discussion at https://gitlab.hzdr.de/hmc/hmc/cct-7-semantics/hmc-glossary-initialization/-/merge_requests/88"@en ,
                                                                     """We re-arranged the approach to structuredness which will now be modeled as a quality. 
A class `structure` at this level of generality is not required for HDO""" ;
                                                        rdfs:label "obsolete Struktur"@de ,
                                                                   "obsolete structure"@en ;
                                                        owl:deprecated "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "Strukturen"@de ,
                                                                                                                "structures"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Struktur"@de ,
                                                                                                                "structure"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000042
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000042> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000009> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Data which an agent has declared as the main focus of a process."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Daten, die durch einen Agenten als Fokus eines Prozesses festgelegt wurden."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym> "data of interest"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/subject> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/subject> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "This class has been created to distinguish data based on the intentionality of one or more agents. Data becomes the \"subject\" of those processes when the agent determines it to be so, prior to or during the process. This becomes especially useful when, for example, a data structure has multiple components bearing data with different roles such as subject data and metadata. "@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Subjektdaten"@de ,
                                                                   "subject data"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "Subjektdaten"@de ,
                                                                                                                "subject data"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000043
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000043> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000047> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "An identifier which some agent has committed to maintain - in the long term - as a valid reference to an entity."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Ein Identifier, für den ein Akteur sich verpflichtet hat, ihn als gültige Referenz auf eine Entität - über einen langen Zeitraum - zur Verfügung zu stellen und zu erhalten."@de ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003012> "PI"@en ,
                                                                                                     "PID"@en ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://datascience.codata.org/articles/10.5334/dsj-2017-009/> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.forschungsdaten.org/index.php/Persistent_Identifier> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.rd-alliance.org/system/files/PID-report_v6.1_2017-12-13_final.pdf> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "In this definition, we are attempting to maintain enough generality to include PIDs which are used in non-networked systems. The agents maintaining persistent identifiers can be diverse, for example, http://hdl.handle.net/ or http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/ "@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "persistent identifier"@en ,
                                                                   "persistenter Identifier"@de ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A persistent identifier is a long-lasting reference to an object. Some persistent identifiers are linked to kernel information profiles which provide metadata or information about that object when the persistent identifier is resolved."@en ,
                                                                                                   "Ein persistenter Identifier ist ein dauerhafter Verweis auf ein Objekt. Einige persistente Identifier sind mit Kerninformationsprofilen verknüpft, die Metadaten oder Informationen über das Objekt liefern, wenn dieser persistente Identifier aufgelöst wird."@de ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "persistent identifiers"@en ,
                                                                                                                "persistente Identifier"@de .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000044
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000044> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "OBSOLETE. A specification which is expressed in a formal language and defines (1) the set of valid values a member of a data type can assume, and (2) the set of valid operations that can be carried out on a member of that data type."@en ,
                                                                                                     "OBSOLETE. Eine Spezifikation, die in einer formalen Sprache ausgedrückt ist für einen Datentyp definiert (1) welche gültigen Werte dieser annehmen, und (2) welche gültigen Operationen mit diesem durchgeführt werden können."@de ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Abstract data type is included in data type as a narrow synonym." ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0100001> <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000007> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003012> "ADT"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_data_type> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-66940000-7> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://opendsa-server.cs.vt.edu/ODSA/Books/CS3/html/Glossary.html#term-abstract-data-type> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://services.informatik.hs-mannheim.de/~schramm/ads/files/Kapitel08.pdf> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://web.mit.edu/6.005/www/fa16/classes/11-abstract-data-types/> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/abstract-data-types/> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.tutorialspoint.com/abstract-data-type-in-data-structures> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> "data type"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> "data type model"@en ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Abstract data types are theoretical constructs, agnostic to implementation environment and intended to support logically coherent, conceptual development of abstract algorithms or other digital assets. In that sense, they abstract the type of data from the use of that data (e.g. in a programme or algorithm). They can be represented in a wide variety of ways, but offer generalisable properties against which any given implementation can be validated. In the context of a programming language, an abstract data type can specify basic types of data (i.e. boolean, real, char) and related stuctures (i.e. array, struct), as well as more idiosyncratic constructs."@en ,
                                                                     "Abstract data type is included in data type as a narrow synonym." ;
                                                        rdfs:label "obsolete abstract data type"@en ,
                                                                   "obsolete obsolete_abstrakter Datentyp"@de ;
                                                        owl:deprecated "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "abstract data types"@en ,
                                                                                                                "abstrakte Datentypen"@de .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000045
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000045> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000048> ;
