###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001006
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001006> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000007> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "An abstract data type which specifies how a symbolic representation is associated with a computational value that may change over time."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Ein abstrakter Datentyp welcher spezifiziert wie eine symbolische Repräsentation (z.B. String) mit einem über die Zeit veränderlichem Wert assoziiert ist. "@de ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000> "var"@de ,
                                                                                                     "var"@en ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385> ,
                                                                                                      <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5077-7497> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym> "Variable"@de ,
                                                                                                                       "variable"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variable_(computer_science)> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "This term can be defined on very different levels. On (1) an general, abstract level (2) at the level of the specification within a given programming language (e.g. \"JAVA variable\") (3) at the level of an instance that is used in a specific piece of code (e.g. $foo). The definition here aims at the most general level, the others can be defined if necessary. A key concept is the fact that a variable maintains its identity while the associated value may change over time (i.e. when a computer program is executed and running). How this is (technically) achieved on implementation level (on the level (2) & (3)) is programming language specific. "@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Computervariable"@de ,
                                                                   "computational variable"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "Computervariable"@de ,
                                                                                                                "Computervariablen"@de ,
                                                                                                                "computational variables"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Computervariable"@de ,
                                                                                                                "computational variable"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001007
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001007> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A disposition which inheres in data and which is realised when that data is accurately identified through a digital system's search or discovery functions."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Eine Veranlagung von Daten, die realisiert wird, wenn diese Daten präzise durch die Suchfunktionen eines digitalen Systems identifiziert werden."@de ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discoverability> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> "Discoverability"@en ,
                                                                                                                       "Findbarkeit"@de ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Queries to find data may be either primarily directed towards associated metadata (i.e. most likely when it comes to larger data sets with complex structure) or directed towards the data itself (i.e. most likely in cases where data can be easily exposed as text). An example for the latter might be the search for a specific gene sequence. The result of such a query might then however be connected to metadata for further filtering the results. This definition is for the findability of data in a general sense. A more specific situation applies to findability according to the FAIR principles which is defined elsewhere. "@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Auffindbarkeit"@de ,
                                                                   "findability"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Das Potential von Daten, durch eine Abfrage nach ihnen selbst oder ihren Metadaten entdeckt zu werden."@de ,
                                                                                                   "The potential of data to be accurately identified as a result of a query towards it or its metadata."@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Auffindbarkeit"@de ,
                                                                                                                "Findability"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001008
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001008> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001007> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Auffindbarkeit, welche Daten zu eigen ist, die (1) mit einem persistenten global eindeutigen Identifier und (2) mit umfangreichen Metadaten assoziiert sind."@de ,
                                                                                                     "Findability which inheres in data that is associated with (1) a globally unique persistent identifier and (2) rich metadata."@en ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://www.go-fair.org/fair-principles/> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata201618.pdf> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> "Findbarkeit im Sinne der FAIR Prinzipien"@de ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Please refer to the definition of \"rich metadata\" as well as general \"findability\" defined elsewhere."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Auffindbarkeit entsprechend den FAIR-Prinzipien"@de ,
                                                                   "findability according to the FAIR principles"@en ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Das Potential von Daten, genau gefunden zu werden, aufgrund (1) ihrer Zuordnung zu einem weltweit eindeutigen, persistenten Identifier, der weitere Suchvektoren eröffnet, (2) ihrer Beschreibung durch umfangreiche Metadaten, (3) ihrer eindeutigen Zuordnung zu diesen umfangreichen Metadaten und (4) ihrer Registrierung in durchsuchbaren Ressourcen."@de ,
                                                                                                   "The potential of data to be accurately discovered due to (1) its association with a persistent globally unique identifier that opens additional search vectors, (2) its description by rich metadata, (3) its unambiguous association with that rich metadata and (4) it being registered or indexed in searchable resources."@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Auffindbarkeit entsprechend den FAIR-Prinzipien"@de ,
                                                                                                                "findability according to the FAIR principles"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001009
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001009> rdf:type owl:Class ;
