                                                                        ] ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A continuant which realises a tool role."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Ein continuant, die eine Rolle als Werkzeug realisiert."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://casrai-test.evision.ca/glossary-term/tool/> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tool> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasNarrowSynonym> "digital tool"@en ,
                                                                                                                        "digitales Tool"@de ,
                                                                                                                        "digitales Werkzeug"@de ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "A tool might extend the capability of a user and/or give it the capability to perform a process that is not possible without it. Tools are not part of the entity (i.e. Input) that an action is performed on (i.e. a wrench is not part of the car) and are typically not consumed during the process."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Werkzeug"@de ,
                                                                   "tool"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "Werkzeuge"@de ,
                                                                                                                "tools"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Werkzeug"@de ,
                                                                                                                "tool"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001016
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001016> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000428> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "OBSOLETE. A collection of tools which is intended for a particular purpose."@en ,
                                                                                                     "OBSOLETE. Eine Sammlung von Werkzeugen, die für einen bestimmten Zweck vorgesehen ist."@de ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0100001> <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001015> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/tooling> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> "Toolbox"@de ,
                                                                                                                         "tool box"@en ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "The purpose can be to assist an agent in accomplishing a specified set of objectives e.g. within a planned process. The term \"tooling\" is also used with alternative meaning e.g. when describing the process of getting or making the right tools or equipment for a particular purpose. Within the scope of this glossary (digital assets & software) there are however more precise terms (\"programming\" vs. \"tooling a software\"). For that reason, we intend to use the term strictly in the sense of the here given definition. TODO: ongoing discussion at https://gitlab.hzdr.de/hmc/hmc/cct-7-semantics/hmc-glossary-initialization/-/merge_requests/61/diffs#82954dcd4b7d149e4f52b3a0df51f3e2cb416c4b"@en ,
                                                                     "We deem that it is not used primarily in digitization context (commonly in the manufacturing." ;
                                                        rdfs:label "obsolete Werkzeugsammlung"@de ,
                                                                   "obsolete tooling"@en ;
                                                        owl:deprecated "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "Werkzeugsammlungen"@de ,
                                                                                                                "tooling"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Werkzeugsammlung"@de ,
                                                                                                                "tooling"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001017
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001017> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001049> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A system which consists of components that are digital."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Ein System welches aus digitalen Einzelteilen besteht."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> "software system"@en ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "A digital system could be a digital repository which consists of digital components such as a database management system and a database."@en ,
                                                                     "The terms software system and digital system are very close but not the same, specifically because most software consists of multiple components and could be seen as a software system. We note however that first, a digital system might also include digital components that are not software (such as data); second the term software system is generally used for the congregation of a software (which is a specification) such as a specific instance of a software running somewhere; and third the term system (as in software system versus software) is generally used for entities with increasing complexity - the threshold for which is arbitrary. For these reasons we keep the terms software and digital system separate in the ontology with software system being a related synonym of digital system."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Digitales System"@de ,
                                                                   "digital system"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001024> "Digitale Systeme"@de ,
                                                                                                                "digital systems"@en ;
                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001026> "Digitales System"@en ,
                                                                                                                "digital system"@en .


