###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001073
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001073> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000019> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A quality which inheres in an entity, by virtue of its properties being defined in a specification which is not publicly released."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Eine Qualität, die einer Entität dadurch innerwohnt, dass ihre Eigenschaften in einer Spezifikation definiert sind, die nicht öffentlich zugänglich ist."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> "proprietary"@en ,
                                                                                                                       "proprietär"@de ;
                                                        rdfs:label "proprietariness"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001074
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001074> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001078> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A file format which is proprietary."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Ein Dateiformat, welches proprietär ist."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C85871" ,
                                                                                                                 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proprietary_file_format" ,
                                                                                                                 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proprietary_file_format#Prominent_proprietary_formats" ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Proprietary formats are typically used by instrument and/or software vendors to store and process data in specific (e.g. efficient, or intentionally inaccessible) ways for a given application. Intentional or not, data encoding in proprietary data formats - to which the specification is unknown - typically results in data and metadata access being impaired or impossible. There are cases where proprietary data formats were opened after some time, i.e when introducing a new version of the proprietary specification. Examples of open proprietary formats are doc and mp3."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Proprietäres Dateiformat"@de ,
                                                                   "proprietary file format"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001075
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001075> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "OBSOLETE Information which identifies the copyrights a resource is released under."@en ,
                                                                                                     "OBSOLETE Informationen welche identifizieren unter welchen Urheberrechten eine Ressource freigegeben ist."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#consider> <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001076> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> "copyright statement"@en ;
                                                        rdfs:comment """This is class is obsolete because we decided to integrate it as an object property 
that relates the class 'copyright' to an entity.""" ;
                                                        rdfs:label "obsolete Copyright Information"@de ,
                                                                   "obsolete copyright information"@en ;
                                                        owl:deprecated "true"^^xsd:boolean .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001076
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001076> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "Legal right which inheres in an entity by virtue of being the owner, creator or inventor of another entity, and which permits the first entity to (1) copy, alter, delete, or reuse the other entity and to (2) pass on copyrights in full or partially to a third entity."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Recht, das einer Entität dadurch zusteht, dass es Eigentümer, Schöpfer oder Erfinder einer anderen Entität ist, und das (1) das Kopieren, Verändern, Löschen oder Wiederverwenden dieser Entität, und (2) die vollständige oder teilweise Weitergabe der Urheberrechte an eine dritte Entität erlaubt."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> "Copyright"@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> "copright information"@en ,
                                                                                                                         "copyright statement"@en ;
                                                        rdfs:comment """Copyright is intended to secure the ideal and commercial interest of an entity over its intellectual property. That is typically an entity being the creator of another entity, for example the author typically holds the copyright for a text written by him/her.
In research, expecially in cases of research data that is recorded in large infrastructures copyright is often not held soly by the creator of the data but also by the insittution where the data was recorded, the owner of the instruments that were used to record the data, or else. In these cases copyright might and should be pre-determined through explicit agreement (e.g. within employment or usage contracts) and be made explicit through licnensing of the data.
Copyright is a legal matter, and this class and its definition are not authoritative."""@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Urheberrecht"@de ,
                                                                   "copyright"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001077
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001077> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001017> ,
                                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                          owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> ;
                                                                          owl:someValuesFrom <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000005>
                                                                        ] ,
                                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                          owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> ;
                                                                          owl:someValuesFrom <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00000029>
                                                                        ] ,
                                                                        [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                          owl:onProperty <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> ;
                                                                          owl:someValuesFrom <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001023>
                                                                        ] ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A digital system which comprises structured data, (meta)data, and software and which allows a computer to store, organise, and access structured data."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Ein digitales System welches aus strukturierten Daten, (Meta)daten und Software besteht und das es einem Computer erlaubt, strukturierte Daten zu speichern, zu organisieren und auf diese zuzugreifen."@de ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_system> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Metadata stored in a file system is associated with files and may include the file name, the length of the contents of a file, and the location of the file in the folder hierarchy—separate from the contents of the file. A file system differs from other forms of data management systems (e.g a database management system) in that file systems supports and/or requires, e.g., filenames, filename extensions, magic numbers, and other unique components. These components result in markedly different user experiences when accessing structured data through such systems."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Dateisystem"@de ,
                                                                   "file system"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001078
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001078> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> ,
                                                                        <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00001005> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A specification which defines how data is to be serialized as a defined unit for handling within a file system."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Eine Spezifikation, die festlegt, wie Daten als definierte Einheit für die Handhabung in einem Dateisystem serialisiert werden sollen."@de ;
                                                        rdfs:comment """A file format specifies serialization for storage. There are data formats like XML, JSON that can be stored with file name extensions and therefore might in practice be used in the sense of a file format.

On a hardware-level, parts of a file might be stored in different locations in a discontinuous fashion. Typically files follow a defined file format to be usable by software and may include a file signature that minimally identifies the file format. Files are typically handled with some file system. For digital files that would typically be the file system of the operating system."""@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Dateiformat"@de ,
                                                                   "file format"@en .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002001
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002001> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002008> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000114> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000125> ;
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A vocabulary which only includes terms that have been deliberately selected by its authors and/or maintainers."@en ,
                                                                                                     "Ein Vokabular, welches nur Begriffe enthält, die mit Absicht durch die Verantwortlichen ausgewählt wurden."@de ;
                                                        <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2209-9385> ;
                                                        <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Controlled_vocabulary> ,
                                                                                                                 <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Controlled_vocabulary#In_library_and_information_science> ;
                                                        rdfs:comment "The methodology used to construct a controlled vocabulary should be documented to verify that the term collection is indeed controlled by it. Controlled vocabularies should address the issues with homographs, synonyms and polysemes by a bijection between concepts and authorized terms. In short, controlled vocabularies reduce ambiguity inherent in normal human language where the same concept can be given different names and ensure consistency."@en ;
                                                        rdfs:label "controlled vocabulary"@en ,
                                                                   "kontrolliertes Vokabular"@de ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A vocabulary which only includes terms that have been deliberately selected by its creators or maintainers. "@en ,
                                                                                                   "Ein Vokabular, welches nur Begriffe enthält, die durch die Verantwortlichen gezielt ausgewählt wurden."@de .


###  https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002002
<https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002002> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf <https://purls.helmholtz-metadaten.de/hob/HDO_00002006> ;
